# Later rules win, so the general normalization comes first and the byte-exact exceptions after it.

# Keep the working tree on LF everywhere, so a byte comparison written on one platform means the
# same thing on the other.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The contract tree is digest-pinned: its exact bytes ARE the contract. Inventory entries record a
# byte length and a SHA-256 per file, the capture commit hashes the canonical JSON, and the
# container golden is compared byte for byte. End-of-line conversion on a Windows checkout would
# silently invalidate every one of those digests, so nothing here may be treated as text.
contract/** -text

# The canonical container fixture is a stored ZIP; keep git from ever converting or diffing it.
*.jazz-archive binary
